{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Everyday Things"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "How Often Does She Work?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "Beginner"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking Questions with When"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "example", "content": " When is the class? "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You ask questions with <span class=\"strong\"> When</span> to know the time, day or date of an activity. <br/> <span class=\"strong\"> When</span> is the first word in the question. <br/>It is followed by the verb <span class=\"strong\"> to be</span> or a form of <span class=\"strong\"> do</span>.<br/><br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When + verb to be + subject ... ?<br />When + do /does + subject + verb ... ?<br/><br/>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When do you start yoga?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When does your class finish?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When are the rooms open?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When does the library open?"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Asking Questions with How Often and How Long"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">James:</span> How often does your sister swim? </br> <span class=\"strong\"> Alex:</span> Once a week. <br/><span class=\"strong\">James:</span> How often do you swim?</span> </br><span class=\"strong\"> Alex:</span> Twice a week."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You ask <span class=\"strong\"> How often</span> to know the frequency of an activity.<br/> You ask<span class=\"strong\">  How long</span> to know the duration of an activity. <br/>These words are followed by <span class=\"strong\"> do </span> or <span class=\"strong\"> does </span> or the verb  <span class=\"strong\"> to be</span>. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">James:</span> How long is the class?</span> </br><span class=\"strong\"> Alex:</span> The class is 1 hour long."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "activity"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a thing that a person or group does"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Yoga is a new activity for me."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le04ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when talking about activities."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "yoga"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a form of body movement and meditation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I like yoga. I do it often."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le04ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "every day"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "each day; daily"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sarah goes to work every day."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le04ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "How long...?"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "question asking for duration of time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(pronoun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How long is the class?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le04ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "It's... long"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "Expression used to talk about the duration of an activity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: <spa